"comparison": "Both Qualcomm and Intel frame their AI strategies around software optimization and framework interoperability to support generative AI, though they differ in specific initiatives. Qualcomm emphasizes running core AI capabilities on-device through its R&D focus, stating, \"We conduct broad, leading research and development across AI, including generative AI, from fundamental research to platform and applied research, with the goal of advancing AI core capabilities to run on-device, and scaling them across industries and use cases.\" In contrast, Intel highlights its role in optimizing open-source frameworks and launching enterprise platforms, noting, \"We aim to optimize AI frameworks and middleware, such as PyTorch, TensorFlow, vLLM, Hugging Face and WebNN to run efficiently on our hardware\" and \"In 2024 we launched the Open Platform for Enterprise AI under the Linux Foundation to accelerate deployment of generative AI use cases through industry standard modular microservice architecture.\"",
